<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kingdom of East Anglia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 6th century–869</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kingdom of East Anglia was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-saxons">Anglo-Saxon</a> kingdom of the East <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angles">Angles</a>, covering modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norfolk">Norfolk</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suffolk">Suffolk</a>, from the sixth century until 869. Its early king Rædwald was overlord of the southern English, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sutton-hoo">Sutton Hoo</a> ship burial is probably his. Often under Mercian overlordship, it regained independence after killing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beornwulf-of-mercia">Beornwulf of Mercia</a> in 826, and fell to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-heathen-army">Great Heathen Army</a>, which killed King Edmund in 869.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-east-anglia.jpg" alt="Kingdom of East Anglia" width="320" height="282" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Amitchell125 at English Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Williamson_p16_3.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
